<title>MALAYSIA: Foreign demand for Malaysia property slows - govt.</title>
<headline>Foreign demand for Malaysia property slows - govt.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overseas demand for luxury real estate in Malaysia fell in the first seven months of 1996 mainly due to a 100,000 ringgit levy imposed in the 1996 budget on foreign purchases, the Finance Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The value of residential properties bought by foreigners declined by 52.2 percent during the first seven months of 1996,&quot; the ministry said in its annual Economic Report.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom 603-201-4813</p>
